.TH "GLESHA-HELP" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-help \- show command options and examples
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha help [COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without a command, show general help. With a command, show its options and examples.
The catalog operations pull, push, reconcile and abandon accept a second help word.
Help does not load configuration, read credentials or contact providers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-L STRING
debug, info, warn, error or silent (default "info")
.TP
.B \-\-color STRING
yes, no or auto; always/never aliases accepted (default "auto")
.TP
.B \-\-config STRING
TOML configuration file
.TP
.B \-\-env STRING
explicit credential environment file
.TP
.B \-\-help
show help
.TP
.B \-h
Alias for \-\-help.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level STRING
debug, info, warn, error or silent (default "info")
.TP
.B \-\-version
show version; \-version is also accepted.
.TP
.B \-v
Alias for \-\-version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha help

glesha help run

glesha help catalog pull
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1)
